__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# The control plane writes LIVE AWS credentials (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / SECRET /
# SESSION_TOKEN, via SSM) into environment/.env inside this checkout. The file is
# 0600 and root-owned, so it is invisible in a casual listing and survives until
# one `git add -A` puts live keys in a public repository. Deny the whole class.
.env
*.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# environment/dist/ is TRACKED, deliberately. It is the compiled reward adapter
# the platform actually runs, the env's provision.sh does NOT build it (Python
# only), and env-publish ships whatever is in the working tree. Gitignoring it
# meant a stale dist could ship silently against fresh source -- which is exactly
# how a breadth-floor change to index.ts went to production with the old compiled
# check still in dist, erroring a rollout at grade time. Committing dist with its
# source makes the two reviewable together and lets a test catch drift.
environment/node_modules/
grader/harness.json
workspace/dev/
# rollout_analysis/artifacts/ is TRACKED. It was ignored, which quietly made every
# citation in this directory unverifiable: the analyses name transcripts and
# submitted solutions as their evidence, and nobody but the author who ran the
# rollout had the bytes. A forensic record that lives on one laptop is a claim,
# not evidence -- and the whole point of these reports is that they are checkable.
# The cost is ~2.6 MB of jsonl and zips, which is nothing against re-running a
# $50 cohort to answer a question the logs already answered.
